WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.127 --> 00:00:18.448
the next morning, Tom and I searched the rubbish heap in the backyard and found an old tin

2
00:00:18.508 --> 00:00:23.270
washtub. We decided that we could use it to bake our big pie in.

3
00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.471
We hid it in the hut, and then went into the house.

4
00:00:28.771 --> 00:00:31.872
No one was in the kitchen yet, so we borrowed a spoon.

5
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:36.821
Tom said Jim could use it to scratch a sad message on his wall.

6
00:00:38.342 --> 00:00:41.943
Later at breakfast, Aunt Sally looked red-faced and cross.

7
00:00:42.903 --> 00:00:49.144
She said to Uncle Silas, "I've looked everywhere for your clean shirt, but I can't find it."

8
00:00:50.145 --> 00:00:53.586
A piece of cornbread stuck in my throat, and I choked a little.

9
00:00:54.946 --> 00:00:58.027
"That's not the only thing that's gone," she said.

10
00:00:58.047 --> 00:01:01.588
"Somehow I've lost one of my best spoons.

11
00:01:02.164 --> 00:01:04.265
Candles are missing from the cellar, too.

12
00:01:05.285 --> 00:01:07.026
But rats might have taken those.

13
00:01:08.127 --> 00:01:13.209
Silas, I've asked you many times to plug the holes in the cellar so that they can't come

14
00:01:13.389 --> 00:01:19.552
in." Uncle Silas apologized to his wife and said he would plug the holes that day.

15
00:01:20.712 --> 00:01:25.734
Just then, a young black servant came into the kitchen and told Aunt Sally that a sheet was

16
00:01:25.814 --> 00:01:29.756
missing. At that, Aunt Sally grew very angry.

17
00:01:30.536 --> 00:01:32.657
"Out of my kitchen, all of you!"

18
00:01:33.357 --> 00:01:33.797
she yelled.

19
00:01:34.978 --> 00:01:37.959
That night, Tom and I put the sheet back on the line.

20
00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.361
Then we snuck into the closet and took a different sheet.

21
00:01:43.361 --> 00:01:48.564
We kept doing this for several days—taking a sheet from one place and putting one back in the

22
00:01:48.644 --> 00:01:54.606
other. By the end of three days, Aunt Sally was so confused that she didn't know how many

23
00:01:54.706 --> 00:01:55.447
sheets she had.

24
00:01:56.447 --> 00:01:58.588
She stopped complaining about the missing sheet.

25
00:02:00.896 --> 00:02:04.900
We tore up the sheet and braided the strips together to make a rope ladder.

26
00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:08.463
We pretended that it had taken us nine months to make it.

27
00:02:09.443 --> 00:02:13.367
Next we had to bake a pie to hide the ladder in and give it to Jim.

28
00:02:14.348 --> 00:02:16.830
That night, we borrowed flour from the kitchen.

29
00:02:18.331 --> 00:02:23.395
The next day, we took it and the washtub into the woods, and we built a campfire to

30
00:02:23.455 --> 00:02:24.116
bake the pie.

31
00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:28.880
The tub was large, but we needed a big pie to hide our ladder.

32
00:02:30.024 --> 00:02:30.885
It was hard work.

33
00:02:31.465 --> 00:02:35.849
We didn't put anything inside the pie because we wanted to leave room for the ladder.

34
00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:40.933
But the top crust kept collapsing, and we kept having to start again.

35
00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:48.159
Finally, we realized that we had to bake the pie with the ladder already inside, and that is

36
00:02:48.199 --> 00:02:48.680
what we did.

37
00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:53.484
Then we took the huge pie through the hole we'd dug and gave it to Jim.

38
00:02:54.524 --> 00:02:58.628
We told him to be very careful eating the pie, so that he didn't chew the ladder.

39
00:02:59.652 --> 00:03:02.413
And we told him that he should hide the ladder in his mattress.

40
00:03:03.013 --> 00:03:03.573
Jim agreed.

41
00:03:04.914 --> 00:03:07.794
Tom said that he thought our plan was going very well.

42
00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:12.876
But Jim hadn't yet used the spoon to scratch a sad message on the wall.

43
00:03:13.996 --> 00:03:18.757
Tom made a list of things Jim might write, and his voice trembled with emotion when he read

44
00:03:18.797 --> 00:03:21.418
them to me: 1.

45
00:03:22.378 --> 00:03:24.459
Here, a captive heart broke.

46
00:03:25.719 --> 00:03:34.131
2. Here, a poor prisoner, forgotten by the world, lived out his sad life.

47
00:03:34.151 --> 00:03:41.975
3. Here, a lonely soul went to its rest, after 37 years of being a prisoner.

48
00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:47.418
I agreed that they were very sad, but I saw a problem.

49
00:03:48.498 --> 00:03:50.199
He doesn't know how to read or write.

50
00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:55.542
Tom said that he would outline the letters on the wall, and Jim could trace over them.

51
00:03:57.943 --> 00:04:00.185
The next night, we visited Jim again.

52
00:04:01.386 --> 00:04:07.209
Tom told Jim that he really ought to have some spiders, or maybe some rats or snakes, in

53
00:04:07.249 --> 00:04:07.750
his prison.

54
00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:12.392
Tom said that prisoners in books always had creatures like this.

55
00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:15.895
"You could make them your pets," Tom said.

56
00:04:17.075 --> 00:04:20.498
Jim thought this was a very bad idea, and so did I.

57
00:04:21.138 --> 00:04:22.899
But I still didn't stop Tom.

58
00:04:23.479 --> 00:04:24.180
I wish I had.

59
00:04:25.344 --> 00:04:29.988
The next day, we went down to the cellar and opened one of the holes Uncle Silas had

60
00:04:30.029 --> 00:04:36.174
mended. Tom and I caught 16 rats in a wire cage and hid them under our bed.

61
00:04:37.956 --> 00:04:42.280
However, the latch on our cage door popped open, and they all escaped.

62
00:04:43.441 --> 00:04:45.703
It took us quite a while to catch 16 more.

63
00:04:46.804 --> 00:04:50.728
We caught a few garter snakes too, and some of them got free in the house.

64
00:04:51.904 --> 00:04:57.429
The whole family was becoming very nervous, with rats and snakes popping out when they weren't expecting them.

65
00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:03.413
Meanwhile, we also caught spiders, frogs, and caterpillars.

66
00:05:04.694 --> 00:05:06.616
We put all the creatures in Jim's shed.

67
00:05:07.797 --> 00:05:11.740
Every time a rat gave Jim a little nip, he'd make a mark on the shirt in his

68
00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:16.424
blood. Jim was kept very busy satisfying Tom's need for adventure.
